From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: a user's view of the machine's store is read-only (7604)

A user's system store merges the machine's, which was opened for writing
first: for a 32-bit program of a standard user, registry virtualization
gave its empty VirtualStore copy. It is read-only, as Windows'
.LocalMachine physical store is.
---
--- a/dlls/crypt32/store.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/store.c
@@ -958,6 +958,16 @@
             {
                 dwFlags &= ~CERT_SYSTEM_STORE_CURRENT_USER;
                 dwFlags |= CERT_SYSTEM_STORE_LOCAL_MACHINE;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MACHINE_STORE_WRITABLE
+                /* Stained Glass OS 7604: the user's view of the machine's
+                 * store is read-only, as Windows' .LocalMachine physical
+                 * store is. Opened for writing, a 32-bit program of a
+                 * standard user was given its empty VirtualStore copy (3764
+                 * registry virtualization) instead of failing: its Root store
+                 * held 5 roots, not the machine's 249, and GOM Player's
+                 * signatures did not chain (CERT_E_CHAINING). */
+                dwFlags |= CERT_STORE_READONLY_FLAG;
+#endif
                 regStore = CertOpenStore(CERT_STORE_PROV_SYSTEM_REGISTRY_W, 0,
                  0, dwFlags, pvPara);
                 /* Stained Glass OS: a standard user may not write the
